cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LibSync in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "LibSync: an AI assistant for public libraries"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Boutwell
    given-names: Johnnie
repository-code: "https://github.com/JohnnieMaeB/LibSync"
url: "https://johnniemaeb.github.io/LibSync/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  LibSync is an open-source AI assistant for public libraries. It answers
  library-desk questions from a library's own policies and from open catalogs
  (Open Library, OpenAlex, Crossref), says so when it cannot check something,
  and is built to integrate with the systems libraries already run. It runs on
  free tiers (PydanticAI, Groq, Pinecone) and is evaluated weekly against
  known-answer cases. Nearly all of the code is written by Claude Code under
  the author's direction.
keywords:
  - libraries
  - library technology
  - ai agents
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - llm evaluation
  - accessibility
